!! BuzzDark — a minimal flat dark openbox theme for the agent's desktop.
!!
!! Goal: window chrome that looks like a modern app, not the 1980s-Motif
!! default openbox ships with. Flat fills, no bevels/gradients, one accent
!! color. Titlebar button glyphs are hand-shipped .xbm bitmaps (iconify /
!! max / max_toggled / close) drawn Chromium-style: 1px strokes on a 12x12
!! grid. Without them openbox falls back to its tiny built-in glyphs, which
!! read as cheap next to Chromium's own titlebar buttons.
!!
!! There is no window.title.height key in openbox's theme format — an
!! earlier version of this theme set one, which openbox silently ignored
!! (unknown keys are not errors), and the titlebar rendered at whatever
!! height the font's line-height plus padding.height produced: with
!! padding.height left at its default and no font set, that collapsed to
!! ~14px — enough to be visible, not enough to feel like a comfortable
!! drag target. The real controls are padding.height (global internal
!! padding for labels/buttons) and window.font (size drives the titlebar's
!! actual height, since openbox sizes the bar to fit the label). Both are
!! set explicitly below (padding.width sits with the rest of the border
!! settings further down) to produce a ~30px bar.
!! (No font key here: openbox reads titlebar/menu fonts from rc.xml's
!! <theme><font place=...> entries — see sprig-desktop-openbox-rc.xml.)
!!
!! Colors are neutral greys matched to Chromium's dark frame (#282828
!! active), so openbox-decorated windows (Thunar, xfce4-terminal) sit next
!! to Chromium without a visible tint difference — an earlier aubergine
!! tint read as purple beside the browser and was flagged by the user.
window.active.title.bg: flat solid
window.active.title.bg.color: #282828
window.inactive.title.bg: flat solid
window.inactive.title.bg.color: #1f1f1f

!! Titlebar text
window.label.text.justify: center
window.active.label.bg: parentrelative
window.active.label.text.color: #e8e8e8
window.inactive.label.bg: parentrelative
window.inactive.label.text.color: #8f8f8f

!! Titlebar buttons (close / maximize / iconify) — flat, subtle hover only.
window.*.button.*.bg: parentrelative
window.active.button.*.hover.bg: flat solid
window.active.button.*.hover.bg.color: #3a3a3a
window.inactive.button.*.hover.bg: parentrelative
window.*.button.*.pressed.bg: flat solid
window.*.button.*.pressed.bg.color: #464646

window.active.button.*.image.color: #c8c8c8
window.active.button.disabled.image.color: #6e6e6e
window.inactive.button.*.image.color: #6e6e6e
window.inactive.button.disabled.image.color: #3c3c3c

!! Borders — thin, no bevel/handle. window.handle.width: 0 removes the
!! resize-grip strip below the titlebar that reads as dated. padding.width
!! (horizontal) widens each titlebar button around its glyph — 6 spreads
!! the buttons apart like Chromium's; padding.height gives the bar its
!! ~30px height. window.client.padding.* is the separate, unrelated space
!! around the app's own content and stays 0.
window.active.border.color: #3a3a3a
window.inactive.border.color: #1a1a1a
border.width: 1
padding.width: 6
padding.height: 8
window.handle.width: 0
window.client.padding.width: 0
window.client.padding.height: 0

!! Menu — this is the root right-click launcher (New Browser Window /
!! Files / Terminal / Close), the human's only way to open new windows
!! since there's no dock. Generous padding and a real UI font so it reads
!! as a modern app menu, not a stock 1990s window-manager popup. Same
!! neutral greys as the titlebar above.
menu.font: shadow=n:Inter:size=11
menu.title.font: shadow=n:Inter Bold:size=11
menu.items.bg: flat solid
menu.items.bg.color: #232323
menu.items.text.color: #e8e8e8
menu.items.justify: left
menu.items.disabled.text.color: #6e6e6e
menu.title.bg: flat solid
menu.title.bg.color: #1a1a1a
menu.title.text.color: #e8e8e8
menu.title.text.justify: left
menu.items.active.bg: flat solid
menu.items.active.bg.color: #3a3a3a
menu.items.active.text.color: #ffffff
menu.overlap: 0
menu.border.color: #3a3a3a
menu.border.width: 1

!! On-screen displays (e.g. the alt-tab switcher)
osd.bg: flat solid
osd.bg.color: #232323
